<Layout
	title="About Me: Why I Started Decoding The Burn"
	description="The personal story of Denis Ethier, how Burning Mouth Syndrome turned his life upside down, and how self-experimentation led to lasting relief."
	pubDate={pubDate}
	heroImage={authorPhoto}
>
	<div class="about-page">
		<p class="lead" style="font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
			My name is Denis Ethier. I am a software designer, builder, and former chronic Burning Mouth Syndrome (BMS) sufferer. I built <strong>Decoding The Burn</strong> to be the transparent, data-driven guide I desperately needed on the darkest days of my condition.
		</p>

		<h2>The Day the Burning Began</h2>
		<p>
			In early 2025, I woke up with a sensation that felt as if someone had pressed a boiling teaspoon against the tip and edges of my tongue. I initially brushed it off as an accidental burn from hot food. But day after day, week after week, the fire never subsided.
		</p>
		<p>
			By mid-afternoon each day, the pain would climb to an 8/10. Speaking felt like dragging sandpaper across raw tissue. Eating acidic or salty foods became agonizing. And yet, every time I looked in the mirror, my tongue looked completely pink, healthy, and normal.
		</p>

		<h2>The Frustration of "Nothing is Wrong"</h2>
		<p>
			Like almost everyone who develops BMS, I began the standard medical marathon:
		</p>
		<ul style="line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
			<li>My dentist checked for oral thrush, infection, and lesions: <em>Negative.</em></li>
			<li>My doctor ran comprehensive blood panels for B12, folate, ferritin, and autoimmune markers: <em>Normal.</em></li>
			<li>The ENT checked my salivary glands and throat: <em>Nothing to see.</em></li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Hearing that "everything is completely healthy" when you feel like your mouth is on fire is a unique form of psychological torture. You begin wondering if you are losing your mind. That was the moment I realized: <strong>if traditional medicine didn't have an answer, I had to treat my own body as an engineering problem.</strong>
		</p>

		<h2>Treating My Body Like a System</h2>
		<p>
			Coming from a technology and product background, I know that unexplained system failures always have root causes—even if you haven't identified the right telemetry yet.
		</p>
		<p>
			I began logging everything in a meticulous spreadsheet:
		</p>
		<ul style="line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
			<li>Exact sleep times, room humidity, and waking mouth dryness</li>
			<li>Dietary intake, food acidity (pH), and ingredient sensitivities</li>
			<li>Salivary flow rates throughout the day</li>
			<li>Autonomic stress levels and breathwork patterns</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>The Breakthrough</h2>
		<p>
			The watershed moment came when I connected nocturnal mouth breathing to oral mucosal drying. When you sleep with your mouth open, hours of evaporative drying strip away the protective mucin film. The superficial nerve endings (chorda tympani and lingual nerve) become severely hyper-sensitized and irritated.
		</p>
		<p>
			By adopting a strict protocol of gentle nighttime mouth taping, eliminating sodium lauryl sulfate (SLS), and restoring salivary mineral balance, my pain dropped by 80% within a single week. Within a month, my BMS was effectively in complete remission.
		</p>

		<h2>Why I Created Decoding The Burn</h2>
		<p>
			I couldn't just walk away and pretend this never happened. Millions of people around the world are suffering in silence with BMS, being told by specialists to "learn to live with it" or handed heavy neurological medications with severe side effects.
		</p>
		<p>
			I built this platform to:
		</p>
		<ul style="line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
			<li><strong>Document My Experiments:</strong> Transparently share what worked, what failed, and what the latest scientific literature actually says.</li>
			<li><strong>Gather Community Data:</strong> Run structured patient surveys to discover clusters and patterns that clinical studies miss.</li>
			<li><strong>Give Sufferers Hope:</strong> Prove that an invisible condition does not have to be a life sentence.</li>
		</ul>

		<div style="background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid var(--card-border); padding: 3rem 2.5rem; border-radius: 24px; margin: 3.5rem 0; text-align: center; box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);">
